% Test cases for the eye prostheses policy (eye_prostheses.le): synthetic
% claims, one per criterion of LCD L33737 and per payment condition of
% Policy Article A52462, each stating only what its record shows. A
% prosthesis is a purchase: no rental month. The benefit is a prosthetic
% one, so no residence is needed.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base eye prostheses cases includes these resources:
    eye_prostheses.

the knowledge base eye prostheses cases includes:

query pay is:
    which claim is payable.

query rn is:
    which claim is reasonable and necessary.

query stage is:
    the query fails at which section.

query flip is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        claim 1 is payable.

% A complete claim for a custom ocular prosthesis (V2623) after the
% surgical removal of an eye: the condition, the standard written order,
% the delivery and its proof.
scenario complete is:
    claim 1 is for the ocular prosthesis.
    the HCPCS code of the ocular prosthesis is "V2623".
    the ocular prosthesis is furnished to Ann.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    Ann has absence of an eye due to surgical removal.
    the order for the ocular prosthesis is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the ocular prosthesis is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the ocular prosthesis includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the ocular prosthesis includes order date.
    the order for the ocular prosthesis includes description of the item.
    the order for the ocular prosthesis includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the ocular prosthesis includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the ocular prosthesis was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the ocular prosthesis was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the ocular prosthesis.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].

% A scleral cover shell (V2627) for an eye shrunken by trauma.
scenario scleral_shell is:
    claim 1 is for the scleral shell.
    the HCPCS code of the scleral shell is "V2627".
    the scleral shell is furnished to Ben.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    Ben has shrinkage of an eye due to trauma.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% Criterion 1 fails: the record states no absence or shrinkage of an eye.
scenario no_condition is:
    claim 1 is for the ocular prosthesis.
    the HCPCS code of the ocular prosthesis is "V2629".
    the ocular prosthesis is furnished to Cy.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at question"].

% Polishing and resurfacing (V2624): the second in twelve months is covered
% (claim 1), the third is not (claim 2).
scenario polishing is:
    claim 1 is for the second polishing.
    the HCPCS code of the second polishing is "V2624".
    the second polishing is furnished to Dee.
    the second polishing is an accessory of the prosthesis of Dee.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    the number of polishing and resurfacing services on the prosthesis of Dee in the twelve months ending on the date of service of claim 1 is 2.
    the HCPCS code of the prosthesis of Dee is "V2623".
    the prosthesis of Dee is furnished to Dee.
    Dee has absence of an eye due to birth defect.
    claim 2 is for the third polishing.
    the HCPCS code of the third polishing is "V2624".
    the third polishing is furnished to Eve.
    the third polishing is an accessory of the prosthesis of Eve.
    the date of service of claim 2 is 2026-03-01.
    the number of polishing and resurfacing services on the prosthesis of Eve in the twelve months ending on the date of service of claim 2 is 3.
    the HCPCS code of the prosthesis of Eve is "V2623".
    the prosthesis of Eve is furnished to Eve.
    Eve has absence of an eye due to surgical removal.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% The first enlargement (V2625), 120 days after the delivery of the
% prosthesis: covered without documentation.
scenario first_enlargement is:
    claim 1 is for the enlargement.
    the HCPCS code of the enlargement is "V2625".
    the enlargement is furnished to Fay.
    the enlargement is an accessory of the ocular prosthesis.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-07-01.
    the number of enlargements and reductions of the ocular prosthesis previously furnished is 0.
    the HCPCS code of the ocular prosthesis is "V2623".
    the ocular prosthesis is furnished to Fay.
    the ocular prosthesis was delivered on 2026-03-03.
    Fay has absence of an eye due to surgical removal.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% A reduction (V2626) 30 days after delivery: a modification within 90 days
% is included in the allowance of the prosthesis.
scenario modification_within_90_days is:
    claim 1 is for the reduction.
    the HCPCS code of the reduction is "V2626".
    the reduction is furnished to Gus.
    the reduction is an accessory of the ocular prosthesis.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-04-01.
    the number of enlargements and reductions of the ocular prosthesis previously furnished is 0.
    the HCPCS code of the ocular prosthesis is "V2623".
    the ocular prosthesis is furnished to Gus.
    the ocular prosthesis was delivered on 2026-03-02.
    Gus has absence of an eye due to surgical removal.
    rn expects answers [].

% A second enlargement: the treating practitioner finds it necessary
% (claim 1, covered); for another beneficiary the Council finds the record
% does not support it (claim 2, denied).
scenario additional_enlargement is:
    claim 1 is for the enlargement of Hal.
    the HCPCS code of the enlargement of Hal is "V2625".
    the enlargement of Hal is furnished to Hal.
    the enlargement of Hal is an accessory of the prosthesis of Hal.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-09-01.
    the number of enlargements and reductions of the prosthesis of Hal previously furnished is 1.
    the finding additional adjustment medically necessary about Hal is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "the socket has contracted further after radiotherapy and the prosthesis no longer fills it".
    the HCPCS code of the prosthesis of Hal is "V2623".
    the prosthesis of Hal is furnished to Hal.
    the prosthesis of Hal was delivered on 2026-01-15.
    Hal has absence of an eye due to surgical removal.
    claim 2 is for the enlargement of Ida.
    the HCPCS code of the enlargement of Ida is "V2625".
    the enlargement of Ida is furnished to Ida.
    the enlargement of Ida is an accessory of the prosthesis of Ida.
    the date of service of claim 2 is 2026-09-01.
    the number of enlargements and reductions of the prosthesis of Ida previously furnished is 2.
    the finding additional adjustment medically necessary about Ida is unsupported, according to the Council, because "the medical record contains no information supporting the medical necessity of a third enlargement".
    the HCPCS code of the prosthesis of Ida is "V2623".
    the prosthesis of Ida is furnished to Ida.
    the prosthesis of Ida was delivered on 2026-01-15.
    Ida has absence of an eye due to trauma.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% A trial scleral shell (L9900): in scope, but in no benefit — included in
% the allowance for the scleral cover shell.
scenario trial_shell is:
    claim 1 is for the trial shell.
    the HCPCS code of the trial shell is "L9900".
    the trial shell is furnished to Jo.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    Jo has shrinkage of an eye due to trauma.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at applicability"].

% Reasonable and necessary, but no proof of delivery: payable fails at the
% remedy.
scenario no_proof_of_delivery is:
    claim 1 is for the ocular prosthesis.
    the HCPCS code of the ocular prosthesis is "V2623".
    the ocular prosthesis is furnished to Kim.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    Kim has absence of an eye due to surgical removal.
    the order for the ocular prosthesis is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the ocular prosthesis is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the ocular prosthesis includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the ocular prosthesis includes order date.
    the order for the ocular prosthesis includes description of the item.
    the order for the ocular prosthesis includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the ocular prosthesis includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the ocular prosthesis was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the ocular prosthesis was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at remedy"].
    flip expects changes [["add: the supplier holds proof of delivery for the ocular prosthesis"]].
